# ---------- Wastewander camps ----------
A 1690 | Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle in Gadgetzan
A 1707 | Spigot Operator Luglunket, next to Bilgewhizzle
A 2781 | The Wanted poster in Gadgetzan
C 1690,1707,379 @ Tanaris, 62.5, 29.0 | The Wastewander Bandits and Thieves camp east of Gadgetzan (around 59-65, 23-33). Any Wastewander can drop a Water Pouch; you need 10 in all (5 for each quest). Pull 2-3 at a time, then Frost Nova and Blizzard.
L 43 @ Tanaris, 62.5, 29.0 | Quest XP runs short in this segment. Keep clearing the Wastewander Bandits and Thieves in this camp until level 43. Loot every kill: the OOX-17/TN Distress Beacon (it starts a quest later in this segment) is a rare drop from almost any Tanaris mob.
T 1690 | Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle
A 1691 | Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle
T 1707 | Spigot Operator Luglunket. Spare pouches can go to him too if he offers the repeatable bounty.
T 379 | Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle. He gives you the Model 4711-FTZ Power Source. Do NOT right-click it yet: it starts a two-hour timer, so you use it after the level 44 grind.
C 1691,2781 @ Tanaris, 61.8, 37.5 | The second Wastewander camp is south of the first (around 59-66, 33-41): Shadow Mages, Rogues and Assassins. Caliph Scorpidsting stands in the middle of it at 61.8, 38.2. Clear his guards first, then kill him for his head.
L 44 @ Tanaris, 61.8, 37.0 | Keep killing the Shadow Mages, Rogues and Assassins in the south camp until level 44 (you train right after the Gadgetzan hand-ins). The camp respawns quickly, so work in a loop around it.
A 654 @ Tanaris, 58.5, 35.0 | Now right-click the power source at the west edge of the camp. From here you have two hours to collect the samples and hand the kit in, so go straight on.
C 654 @ Tanaris, 55.0, 33.0 | Keep the Field Testing Kit in your bags. On the ride back west to Gadgetzan, kill Glasshide Basilisks, Blisterpaw hyenas and Scorpid Hunters or Tail Lashers; all three roam the flats between the camp and town (about 48-60, 25-40). Loot each one for its sample. Not every sample passes the kit's test, so expect more than 8 kills of each.
T 1691,2781 | Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle
T 654 | Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle
A 864 @ Tanaris, 52.5, 28.5 | Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle. Keep it for the Undercity (later segment).

# ---------- Thunder Bluff: level 44 training ----------
N Teleport: Thunder Bluff (or fly there from Gadgetzan if you don't have it)
T 1205 | Melor Stonehoof on Hunter's Rise
TRAIN | Thunder Bluff, Spirit Rise mage trainers: learn your level 44 spells
H Gadgetzan | Faster than the flight back. If the hearthstone is still on cooldown, fly to Gadgetzan instead.

# ---------- Western and central Tanaris ----------
A 992 | Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser
C 992 @ Tanaris, 39.0, 29.3 | Ride west to Sandsorrow Watch. Use the Untapped Dowsing Widget beside the small pool just south of the Sandfury troll huts. The Sandfury trolls are elite (42-44) and stand just east and north-east of the pool, with two rare elites further north. Swing round and come in from the south-west, use the widget at the pool's west edge and leave at once.
T 992 | Back in Gadgetzan: Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser
A 82 | Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser
C 82 | The Noxious Lair is south-west of Gadgetzan (around 33, 44). The bugs are level 47-50: pull single Tunnelers and Workers from the outer edge (they drop the parts about half the time; Wasps rarely) and do not go deep inside.
A 3161 | Ride east to Marvon Rivetseeker, who camps by the Broken Pillar in central Tanaris (52.7, 45.9)
C 3161 | Put on the Gahz'ridian Detector (head slot) and ride through the desert south-west of Marvon (around 40-48, 60-72); it shows the buried Gahz'ridian mounds. Click a mound to dig up the ornaments. Swap your own helm back on afterwards.
T 3161 | Marvon Rivetseeker
A 351 @ Tanaris, 60.2, 64.7 | Right-click the OOX-17/TN Distress Beacon. It is a rare (about 1%) drop from almost any Tanaris mob: Wastewanders, pirates, beasts and bugs. No beacon yet? Kill Blisterpaw Hyenas, basilisks and scorpids on the ride south-east from Marvon until it drops. If it still has not dropped by the Gaping Chasm, go on without it and do the robot on your next Tanaris visit (next segment).
T 351 | Homing Robot OOX-17/TN, at the edge of the Gaping Chasm (60.2, 64.7)
A 648 | Homing Robot OOX-17/TN
C 648 @ Tanaris, 67.0, 24.0 | Escort the robot north to Steamwheedle Port. Ambushers come out of the sand: kill them fast or the robot dies. If it fails, go back and talk to the robot again.

# ---------- Steamwheedle Port and Lost Rigger Cove ----------
T 2872 | Stoley in Steamwheedle Port
A 2873 | Stoley
A 2875 | The Wanted poster in Steamwheedle Port
A 8366 | Security Chief Bilgewhizzle
A 8365 | Haughty Modiste
A 3520 | Yeh'kinya, beside the Haughty Modiste. Keep it for the next segment: the vale screechers live in Feral Scar Vale in Feralas, and you come back past Yeh'kinya after the Tooga escort.
C 2873,2875,8365,8366 @ Tanaris, 73.5, 46.5 | Lost Rigger Cove, the walled pirate town south down the coast. Stoley's Shipment is the Stolen Cargo near the docks (72.2, 46.8); Andre Firebeard stands at 73.4, 47.1. Every Southsea pirate can drop a hat. Pull small groups out of the walls: Frost Nova, Blizzard, step back. If a Ship Schedule drops, hand it to the Security Chief as well.
L 45 @ Tanaris, 73.5, 46.5 | Stay in Lost Rigger Cove until level 45. The hats are a slow drop, so most of this grind happens on its own, and the pirates come in groups that suit Blizzard.
T 2873 | Stoley
A 2874 | Stoley. Keep it for Booty Bay (next segment).
T 2875,8366 | Security Chief Bilgewhizzle
T 8365 | Haughty Modiste
T 82 | Ride back west along the road to Gadgetzan (or hearth if it is ready): Alchemist Pestlezugg
N Keep these for later segments: 2874 Deliver to MacKinley and 648 Rescue OOX-17/TN (Booty Bay), 864 Return to Apothecary Zinge (Undercity), 1262 Report to Zor (Orgrimmar), 3520 Screecher Spirits (Feralas, back to Yeh'kinya). Your hearthstone stays set to Gadgetzan; the next segment starts here with the flight to Freewind Post.
